{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the full picture:\n\n- 00 · Start Here: FoodWagon food delivery landing page, 1920 wide, light mode, single frame \"01_Home\"\n- 01 · Foundations: Brand colors #F17228 (orange), #FFB30E (yellow), Source Sans Pro\n- 02 · Components: Button (200x60) and Text Field (420x82) symbols at 1:28 and 1:31\n- 04 · Media: All the assets — logo, badges, photos, icons, social logos. All are symbols (components)\n- 03 · Workspace: empty (canvas with no children)\n\nKey media asset component IDs (symbols):\n- 9:49 Badge_App_Store (144x48)\n- 9:25 Badge_Google_Play (162x48)\n- 9:27 Logo_FoodWagon (257x48)\n- 9:28 Photo_CTA_Background (300x200)\n- 9:55 Photo_Hero_Background (581x200)\n- 9:39 Photo_Hero_Noodles (200x200)\n- 9:31 Photo_Discount_1 (237x200)\n- 9:32 Photo_Discount_2 (237x200)\n- 9:51 Photo_Discount_3 (237x200)\n- 9:33 Photo_Discount_4 (237x200)\n- 9:50 Photo_Cheese_Burger (161x200)\n- 9:29 Photo_Crispy_Sandwich (196x200)\n- 9:41 Photo_Pancake (197x200)\n- 9:47 Photo_Thai_Soup (196x200)\n- 9:48 Photo_Toffee_Cake (196x200)\n- 9:30 Photo_Cupcake_Corner (222x200)\n- 9:52 Photo_Donuts_Hut (222x200)\n- 9:54 Photo_Foodworld (222x200)\n- 9:40 Photo_Kuakata_Fried_Chicken (222x200)\n- 9:56 Photo_Pizzahub (222x200)\n- 9:45 Photo_Red_Square (222x200)\n- 9:57 Photo_Ruby_Grill (222x200)\n- 9:46 Photo_Taco_Bay (222x200)\n- 9:34 Photo_Food_Burger (200x200)\n- 9:35 Photo_Food_Chowmein (201x200)\n- 9:36 Photo_Food_Noodles (201x200)\n- 9:37 Photo_Food_Pizza (200x200)\n- 9:38 Photo_Food_Steak (201x200)\n- 9:53 Photo_Food_Sub_Sandwich (201x200)\n- 9:26 Image_App_Mockup (254x320)\n- 9:42 Photo_Promo_Fried_Chicken (375x200)\n- 9:43 Photo_Promo_Pizza (375x200)\n- 9:44 Photo_Promo_Sandwiches (375x200)\n- 9:22 Logo_Facebook (10x20)\n- 9:23 Logo_Instagram (22x22)\n- 9:24 Logo_Twitter (22x18)\n- Icons (24x24 each): 9:3 Icon_Chevron_Left, 9:4 Icon_Chevron_Right, 9:5 Icon_Clock, 9:6 Icon_Discount, 9:7 Icon_Envelope, 9:8 Icon_Heart, 9:9 Icon_Map_Marker, 9:10 Icon_Motorcycle, 9:11 Icon_Quick_Delivery, 9:12 Icon_Search, 9:13 Icon_Shopping_Bag, 9:14 Icon_Star, 9:15 Icon_Step_Enjoy, 9:16 Icon_Step_Location, 9:17 Icon_Step_Order, 9:18 Icon_Step_Payment, 9:19 Icon_Tag, 9:20 Icon_Tracking, 9:21 Icon_User\n- 1:28 Button component (200x60)\n- 1:31 Text Field component (420x82)\n\nI need to use get_design_context to get more details on the Button and Text Field components so I can reuse them. The important part: the components are components (symbols) in the reference pages. To \"reuse\" them, I should create instances of these components in the workspace, or clone them. Since the file is a benchmark copy and the delivery is in 03 · Workspace of the same file, I can create instances directly from these components (they're in the same file). \n\nLet me get design context for the Button (1:28) and Text Field (1:31) to understand their styling. Also get design context for a few icons to understand their structure (fill colors). Actually the instructions said icons are neutral #1A1A1F and can be recolored.\n\nLet me also check what the components look like via get_design_context — that gives detailed XML with fills etc.\n\nPlan for the design:\n\n**Design system (my own):**\n- Brand: #F17228 (primary orange), #FFB30E (secondary yellow)\n- Neutrals: \n  - Text primary: #1A1A1F (near black)\n  - Text secondary: #5C5C66 or #6B6B74\n  - Background: #FFFFFF\n  - Section tint: #FFF6EF or #FEF5EC (warm light), light gray #F7F7F9\n  - Border: #E8E8EE\n- Type scale (Source Sans Pro):\n  - H1: 44/54 Bold\n  - H2: 32/40 Bold\n  - H3: 24/32 Bold\n  - H4/Section title: 28... Let me keep: Display 40, Section 28, Card title 18, Body 14/16, Small 12\n- Spacing: 8-base grid\n- Radius: 12 for cards, 8 for buttons/fields, full for pills\n- Grid: 1920 wide, content 1280 (margins 320?) Actually brief says 1920 wide. Original FoodWagon kit used 1180/1280 content. I'll use content width 1280 centered (margins 320).\n\n**Layout order** (my decision):\n1. Header (sticky-ish top bar): logo left, \"Deliver to: Current Location / Mohammadpur Bus Stand, Dhaka\", search field, Login button\n2. Hero: Photo_Hero_Background as bg strip, left text \"Are you starving?\" + subtitle, Photo_Hero_Noodles right, search card with Delivery/Pickup tabs, address field, Find Food button\n3. Discount cards row: 4 cards (overlapping hero bottom like original)\n4. Deals: 3 promo blocks (Best deals Crispy Sandwiches, Celebrate parties with Fried Chicken, Wanna eat hot & spicy Pizza?)\n5. Featured Restaurants: title + View All, 8 cards in 2 rows of 4\n6. Features strip: Daily Discounts, Live Tracking, Quick Delivery\n7. Popular items: title + prev/next, 5 cards\n8. Search by Food: title + View All + prev/next, 6 category tiles\n9. How does it work: 4 steps\n10. App promo: \"Install the app\" + copy + mockup + badges\n11. CTA: Photo_CTA_Background + \"Are you ready to order with the best deals?\" + Proceed to order button\n12. Footer: cities, company, contact, legal, follow us, newsletter, copyright\n\nWait, let me think about the order more carefully to make a nice flow:\n1. Header\n2. Hero (with search)\n3. Discounts (4 cards, slightly overlapping hero)\n4. Deals (3 promo banners)\n5. Featured Restaurants (8 cards)\n6. Popular items (carousel, 5 cards)\n7. Search by Food (6 categories)\n8. Features (3 items: Daily Discounts, Live Tracking, Quick Delivery)\n9. How does it work (4 steps)\n10. App promo\n11. CTA\n12. Footer\n\nThat's a good flow: browse → restaurants → dishes → categories → why us → how → app → final CTA → footer.\n\n**Components to build in workspace** (reusable components):\n- Btn/Primary (instance of or clone from given Button with my styling? The given Button is \"fixed\" as default Button — I should reuse the given Button component as the base. Actually the brief says \"Default Button, default Text Field\" are fixed/given. So I should use instances of the given Button and Text Field components for CTAs and fields, overriding text where possible. Let me check what the given Button looks like first — get_design_context on 1:28 and 1:31.)\n\nLet me now use use_figma to read the components in detail (read-only). Actually get_design_context is the tool for that. Let me call get_design_context on 1:28 (Button), 1:31 (Text Field), and maybe a couple of icons to know their fill color structure.\n\nActually, get_design_context returns XML with properties. Let me call it for Button and Text Field.\n\nThen I'll build in sections with use_figma:\n1. Create component set in workspace? The task: \"Design all other states, the header, the footer, the navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file.\" So I should create components. Plan:\n   - Section components: Header/NavBar, Footer, HeroSearchCard, DiscountCard, PromoBanner (deal), RestaurantCard, ItemCard (popular), CategoryTile, StepCard, FeatureItem, AppPromo, CTA, RatingBadge, etc.\n   \n   Building everything as components + instances takes more effort but is required for \"Component reuse\" scoring. I'll create master components in a \"Components\" area of the workspace page (e.g., at x=0, y=-2000 or on the side), then place instances in the 01_Home frame.\n\n2. Build 01_Home frame at 1920 wide with auto-layout sections (or fixed positioning). Auto-layout is safer for consistency.\n\nStrategy for implementation with the Plugin API:\n- Load fonts: \"Source Sans Pro\" Regular, SemiBold, Bold, Black (need to check available styles: Regular, Italic, SemiBold, Bold, Black...). Source Sans Pro in Google Fonts has weights: ExtraLight, Light, Regular, SemiBold, Bold, Black (+ italics). In Figma, \"Source Sans Pro\" styles: \"Regular\", \"SemiBold\", \"Bold\", \"Black\", \"Light\", \"ExtraLight\". I'll load Regular, SemiBold, Bold, Black.\n- Get media components: figma.getNodeById(\"9:27\") etc. → they are ComponentNodes. createInstance() them.\n- For icons recolor: instance.children? Icons are components with vector children; recoloring an instance's vector children requires overriding fills on sublayers — possible via instance.findOne(v => v.type === \"VECTOR\").fills = [...]. That works on instances (overrides allowed on fills of sublayers? Overriding fills of nested layers in instances is allowed for properties visible in \"overrides\" — yes, fills of nested vector layers can be overridden via plugin API).\n\nWait — but can I set fills on nested children of an instance? Yes, plugin API allows setting fills on sublayers of instances; it creates overrides.\n\nPhotos: they're components; I'll create instances and resize, with clipsContent via resize and maybe scale. Instances can be resized. Photos are symbol nodes — I could also clone them. Resizing instances: the components have fixed sizes (e.g., 222x200). To fit into cards, I can resize instance and the inner vector will stretch? Depends on constraints. If inner image has constraints SCALE, resizing works nicely. Let me check one photo's design context to see structure.\n\nLet me get design context for a few nodes:\n- 1:28 Button\n- 1:31 Text Field\n- 9:31 Photo_Discount_1 (structure of photo)\n- 9:9 Icon_Map_Marker (structure of icon)\n- 9:27 Logo_FoodWagon\n\nget_design_context returns detailed XML including fills, fonts, etc. Let me call these in parallel.\n\nThen build. Let me do that now.","signature":"2a52d429a65642a885c596e2"}],"id":"74a4f19d-6e7a-464d-b50c-f15c6e60340b","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0cf375fe-7995-4021-9e71-e24c776e8096","uuid":"24ba334a-d274-49a3-a60d-45f62415dfd3","timestamp":"2026-11-02T00:23:45.061Z","thinking_duration_ms":48167}
