isabled\", \"Button / Secondary\", \"Button / Small Yellow\", \"Link / Arrow\" (View All & Proceed to order share it; label override \"View All\"/\"Proceed to order\")\n5. \"Field / Search\" (header), \"Field / Hero Address\", \"Field / Hero Address Focused\"\n6. \"Tabs / Delivery Current\", \"Tabs / Pickup Idle\"\n7. \"Icon Button / Prev\", \"Icon Button / Next\"\n8. \"Card / Discount\", \"Card / Deal\", \"Card / Restaurant\", \"Card / Item\", \"Tile / Category\", \"Card / Step\", \"Item / Feature\"\n9. \"Section / Header\" (title + optional view all + arrows) — maybe too generic; skip, assemble inline.\n10. \"Header / Main\" (header nav)\n11. \"Footer / Main\"\n12. \"Hero / Search Card\"\n\nThat's ~25 masters. Manageable.\n\nPhotos inside card masters: instances of photo components inside component masters (nested instances OK).\n\n**Absolute-positioned overlays in AL frames**: set child.layoutPositioning='ABSOLUTE' (requires parent AL frame with clipsContent as needed).\n\nLet me also consider: **photo resize + radius**: instance.cornerRadius = 12 works (override). Top-only: topLeftRadius etc. supported on frames.\n\nImage scaleMode: check one photo's fill scaleMode via read call — I'll include in first build call: if scaleMode !== 'FILL', set on instance: inst.fills = [{...fill, scaleMode:'FILL'}]. Since fills array on instance can be read then modified. I'll write helper ensureFill(inst) that copies component fill with scaleMode FILL.\n\n**Logo_FoodWagon**: image 257x48 — instance in header at native size (it's on white presumably; header white bg fine).\n\n**CTA background**: Photo_CTA_Background 300x200 image; stretch to 1920x420 with FILL — will crop heavily but fine.\n\n**Hero background**: Photo_Hero_Background 581x200 → stretch 1920x520 FILL.\n\nAlright — also **\"How to work\" point 3**: define type scale, spacing, radii, elevation, grid and apply consistently — done via constants.\n\nPoint: \"**Copy and data must match Fixed data exactly**\" — use verba