{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All business card components created. Now Call C: Header and Footer master components.\n\n**Header / Main** (1920x96): horizontal AL, width FIXED 1920, height FIXED 96, bg white, padding L/R 320, prim SPACE_BETWEEN, counter CENTER, stroke bottom line (strokes all sides... Figma stroke on specific sides: use strokeBottomWeight individual property — supports strokeTopWeight etc. on frames. Set c.strokeBottomWeight=1, others 0).\nChildren:\n- Logo instance (9:27) 257x48.\n- Deliver-to block: row gap 10 center: [Map_Marker 22 orange][column gap 2: \"Deliver to:\" 12 Regular ink40; \"Current Location · Mohammadpur Bus Stand, Dhaka\" 14 SemiBold ink]. Hmm brief: \"Deliver to:\" · Icon_Map_Marker · \"Current Location\" · \"Mohammadpur Bus Stand, Dhaka\". Two-line: line1 \"Deliver to:\" small; line2: \"Current Location\" bold; line3? Put address on line2 after separator? For exactness make three text nodes: col: \"Deliver to:\" (12, ink40); \"Current Location\" (14 SB ink); then address as separate text right of block? Simplest visually: col: \"Deliver to:\" / \"Current Location\"; then divider dot; address \"Mohammadpur Bus Stand, Dhaka\" (14 R ink60). Row: [icon][col][address text]. I'll do: col1: \"Deliver to:\" + \"Current Location\"; separate text node address 14 R ink60, vertically centered. OK.\n- Search field instance (13:48) 360x48.\n- Login row: gap 12 center: [Icon_User 22 ink] + given Button instance (1:28) resized 132x60, text override \"Login\". Given Button 200 wide default; resize instance to 132 wide (text centered). The given Button component's text child is fixed 55 wide \"Button\"; override chars to \"Login\" → text width shrinks? Text autoResize default WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT probably; override chars updates width; AL centers it. Good.\n\n**Footer / Main** (1920 wide): vertical AL bg ink dark #1A1A1F, pad top 64 bottom 32, gap 0, children (inner container 1280):\n- Inner container column gap 40 width 1280.\n- Row A: \"Our top cities\" block: column gap 16: title \"Our top cities\" 18 Bold white; cities text block: 24 cities joined with \" · \" — as wrapped paragraph? Multi-column look: 4 columns of 6: row gap 48: four columns each gap 8 with 6 city names 14 R #B9B9C2. Cities in order: San Francisco, Los Angeles, New York City, Chicago, Columbus, Miami, Washington DC, Orange County, Phoenix, New Mexico, San Diego, Seattle, Atlanta, Las Vegas, Albuquerque, East Bay, Portland, Charlotte, Sacramento, Long Beach, Nashville, Denver, Oklahoma City, New Orleans. 24 cities → 4 cols × 6.\n- Row B: 3 columns + follow: gap 64: Company col (title 18 Bold white \"Company\", links col gap 10: About us, Team, Careers, Blog each 14 R #B9B9C2); Contact col (\"Contact\": Help & Support, Partner with us, Ride with us); Legal col (\"Legal\": Terms & Conditions, Refund & Cancellation, Privacy Policy, Cookie Policy); Follow col: \"Follow Us\" + social row gap 12: three circle buttons 40 (#2A2A31) each containing social logo instance (FB 10x20 white vectors? social logos are 24-ish components with dark vectors — recolor white).\n- Newsletter row: card bg #26262C? On dark bg use panel #242429 radius 14 pad 20, row SPACE_BETWEEN center: text \"Receive exclusive offers in your mailbox\" 16 SB white; row gap 12: [Envelope icon 22 orange] + given Text Field instance (label override \"Email address\"? Brief says field \"Enter Your email\" — label part of given field; set Label chars \"Email\" (or hide). I'll set label to \"Email address\" and placeholder \"Enter Your email\") + given Button instance \"Subscribe\" (resize 160x60).\n  Given Text Field is 420x82 — in footer that's fine.\n- Divider: rect 1280x1 #2E2E35.\n- Copyright: \"All rights Reserved © FoodWagon, 2021\" 13 R #8A8A94 centered.\n\nFooter height ~ 64+40+~150+~140+~130+1+30+32 ≈ 600.\n\n**Hero section** — build inline in assembly (bg photo + absolute noodles). Not a component (it's a section). That's acceptable; but \"business components\" already covered.\n\nSocial logo sizes: FB 10x20, IG 22x22, TW 22x18 — inside 40 circle, centered: circle AL center; instance fills=[]; vectors white.\n\nNewsletter text field: instance of 1:31; override Label chars \"Email address\"? The brief for footer: field \"Enter Your email\" (Icon_Envelope) — placeholder \"Enter Your email\". Label text isn't specified; set Label visible=false? Hiding a child of instance is allowed (visibility override). Then field = just input 56 high + we lose 26px. Instance height stays 82 with hidden label? AL hug — instance is fixed-size component; hiding label leaves gap. Simplest: set Label chars to \"Email address\" — harmless addition, or \"Email\". I'll set \"Email address\".\n\nEnvelope icon placement: left of field inside row.\n\nHeader/Footer masters placed at cy -1500 area (below atoms & cards which end ~-2300+ heights... place() cursor ended somewhere; I'll place header at (0,-1400), footer at (700,-1400) manually.\n\nThen assembly. Let me write Call C now.","signature":"f1b2548090e740a994bc746c"}],"id":"52c277b1-678a-4316-af7c-2392b55be764","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0cf375fe-7995-4021-9e71-e24c776e8096","uuid":"288a9833-d78a-49e0-b025-da76e1a944ae","timestamp":"2026-11-02T00:35:53.122Z","thinking_duration_ms":31646}
